@startuml 06-disconnect
' A dropped connection, and the same player coming back to the same seat.
skinparam shadowing false
title Dropping out and coming back

actor Player
participant Lobby
participant GameController as Controller
participant Game

Player -> Lobby : (the connection closes)
Lobby -> Lobby : forget(connection)
note right of Lobby
  Under the default policy the seat stays,
  unattached, under the old nickname — unless
  that was the last player, in which case the
  table is reclaimed.
end note
Lobby -> Controller : connectionChanged(colour, false)
Controller -> Game : connectionChanged
Controller --> "the others" : ConnectionChanged(away)

loop while they are away and the card asks them
  Game -> Game : answer passively for them
  Controller --> "the others" : TurnSkipped
end

alt nobody else is left
  Game --> Controller : GameSuspended(seconds)
  ... the timeout passes with nobody back ...
  Game -> Game : everybody away gives up
  Game --> Controller : ShipRetired, then scoring
end

== later ==

Player -> Lobby : Login("samuele")
Lobby -> Lobby : the name belongs to a seat in a running game
Lobby --> Player : LoggedIn, JoinedGame
Lobby -> Controller : attach + announceArrival
Controller -> Game : connectionChanged(colour, true)
Controller --> Player : StateChanged
note right of Controller
  The whole picture, including the question
  the card is still waiting on. A board alone
  would leave them looking at a flight that
  appears to have stopped for no reason.
end note
Controller --> "the others" : GameResumed
@enduml
